{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792415480,"nonce":"G85iZ/VibzTaET7EWa+CSwJ8Cx4=","message":"Stage G is committed on main:\n- RayDE 38a194f343d30388243fe6737ba40865510ba56d\n- RayScript documentation 4edcf85b32862151e458098fcddd8bfcb13074a6\n\nUser selected libgit2 v1.9.7 with system OpenSSH (USE_SSH=exec). scripts/build-libgit2.sh pins the official release archive with SHA-256 1a4fbe7589e814777ae76b64734ad80f4ecad22cd33a22682a2aaea4ae5375e7. The single source/archive/CMake build cache is under RayDE/.deps; the shared library and upstream notices stage under extensions/git/natives, excluded from source control. Build uses bundled zlib/regex, shared libraries, no CLI/tests/examples, and disables the experimental SHA-256 ABI. macOS/Linux packaging invokes the build before copying extensions. On this macOS arm64 machine otool reports only system dependencies. Linux packaging changes were syntax checked, not executed.\n\nextensions/git/ext/gitNative.rays provides repository discovery above the project path, indexed status with rename/conflict information, raw git_status_foreach visitors, staged and workdir diffs through all four git_diff_foreach callbacks, unborn-HEAD handling and native error reporting. Native handles retain owners and are explicitly closed on success and exceptions; callback-scoped views are copied into script records, including length-delimited line Bytes. Scans/diff generation run through blocking lanes and Krio fibers. The normal inspect path uses indexed status; diagnostic callback status is a separate API.\n\nscripts/check-git.sh builds the pin and runs real-host grants with the staged library. The check creates disposable repositories under bin/git-native-checks, tests pinned C layouts, native version/SSH feature, discovery from a child folder, clean/modified/staged/deleted/untracked/ignored/renamed/conflicted paths, staged and workdir hunks/lines, UTF-8 and binary content, unborn HEAD, native failure recovery, deferred callback exceptions, GC/retained copies and concurrent Krio script fibers. All final checks pass. RayDE scripts/check.sh also passed. Shell syntax and git diff --check passed. No Rust runtime changes or additional Cargo builds were needed.\n\nPerformance evidence (release host, 10,000 modified files; five warm samples per median, protocol roundtrip included): indexed status first measured 333.4 ms, a follow-up 236.2 ms. Thus the proposed M2 250 ms budget is not reliably established. A separate raw statusFlags visitor measurement was 18,948.8 ms, recorded for native-to-script callback profiling/fiber pooling. No claims of a passing performance gate. The Git M2 issue remains open.\n\nLogs: /tmp/libgit2-g-build.log, /tmp/git-g-final.log (includes first benchmark), /tmp/git-g-final-functional.log (final functional run), /tmp/rayde-g-checks.log. Captured structured result: RayDE/bin/git-native-checks/snapshot.json. Docs: RayDE/docs/git.md and RayScript/docs/native.md.\n\nThis completes the initial macOS arm64 FFI stages A-G and the real-library integration exit criterion. No visible RayDE UI change in Stage G, so no new snapshots under the user's preference. There is not yet an installed Git manifest or SCM UI: the next read-only Git milestone consumes this backend. Asked whether the first SCM sidebar should use RayScript extension UI (recommended) or native Haxe; no answer yet. The newer Git issue already specifies a CodeEditor diff fallback. Hook and credential decisions remain for later mutation/network milestones.\n\nBoth canonical main checkouts are clean, one worktree each. No extra Cargo target directories, no code or bug refs pushed. No completion/language files or other sibling repositories changed.","files":null}]}